<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Backstory!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Robert Difortune was Leonard's uncle, who had killed his father many years ago but was acquitted due to the money (and muscle) of the Gambino family, of which he was associated with. Thus, Leonard had a hatred of organized crime.<br />
Robert in fact was the first victim of this SCP, and upon learning of the property of the gun after finding his father alive and his journal bearing entries of a childhood he does not remember, Leonard decidees to use it to &quot;rid New York of its underground elite.&quot;. 'Course, things do not always work out, and Leonard ends up having to kill many people. And the strong weather ain't a coincidence&#8230;</p>
<p>As for who shot Leonard? Well, that, I intend to leave open-ended. Nonetheless, I can offer two opinions:</p>
<p>1) The Irish mob exists in the future, and they have gone anomalous. Their biggest heist so far is when they stole a whole bunch of chrono-anomalous SCPs&#8230;<br />
2) The Foundation, in desperation against the DEAD-CHRONOS event, has authorized the use of SCPs to avert the damaging of retrocausality without causing too much damage in the process&#8230;</p>
